+# Why every field is pill-shaped
+
+## The mechanism — what consumes `--radius-field`
+
+`--radius-field` is not your CSS. It's a **daisyUI 5 theme token**. daisyUI 5
+ships three corner-radius tokens, each scoped to a family of components:
+
+- `--radius-selector` → checkbox, toggle, radio, badge
+- `--radius-field` → **input, select, textarea, btn, tab, file-input, join items**
+- `--radius-box` → card, modal, alert, menu
+
+Every daisyUI component in the "field" family sets its corners *from the token*,
+roughly:
+
+```css
+.input, .select, .textarea, .btn { border-radius: var(--radius-field); }
+```
+
+Scaffold-ETH 2's inputs (`InputBase`, `AddressInput`, the RainbowKit/daisyUI
+form controls, etc.) all carry those daisyUI component classes. So they never
+hardcode a radius — they *inherit* whatever the active theme sets `--radius-field`
+to.
+
+You set it to `9999rem`. A border-radius that large clamps to "half the shorter
+side," i.e. a full semicircle on each end → **pill shape** for single-line inputs.
+On a multi-line `textarea` the same 9999rem is applied to all four corners, and
+because the box is tall the huge quarter-circles eat into the top and bottom edges
+— that's the **corner clipping** of the text.
+
+One token, read by every field component in the app, is why *all* of them
+reshape at once. It's a single source of truth working exactly as designed — just
+pointed at a broken value.
+
+## Why the per-component `rounded-*` patching keeps losing
+
+The patch (`rounded-lg` on individual inputs) doesn't fight the token — it
+sidesteps it on exactly the elements you remembered to touch. That loses for two
+reasons:
+
+1. **Default is still broken.** `rounded-lg` only sets `border-radius` on that one
+   element. The theme token `--radius-field: 9999rem` is untouched, so it stays the
+   *default* for every field. Every new form field the team adds inherits the
+   default again → pill. You're playing whack-a-mole against a default that keeps
+   reasserting.
+
+2. **Drift.** The patched inputs are now hardcoded to `0.5rem` (`rounded-lg`),
+   disconnected from the theme. They no longer track the token that the rest of
+   the design system flows from, so when anything else about the field styling
+   changes, the two patched inputs drift out of sync. You've created two
+   exceptions instead of one correct rule.
+
+Fixing the token fixes the default for every current and future field at once, and
+lets you *delete* the `rounded-lg` patches so nothing is special-cased.
+
+## The correct fix
+
+Set the token to a sane radius instead of patching components. To match the
+`rounded-lg` the teammate already reached for (and daisyUI's own default), use:
+
+```css
+--radius-field: 0.5rem;
+```
+
+(Use whatever the design calls for — `0.375rem` / `0.25rem` etc. — the point is a
+finite value, not `9999rem`.)
+
+**Where to apply it — every theme block in this file.** daisyUI theme tokens are
+defined *per theme*. Scaffold-ETH 2's `globals.css` declares **two**
+`@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks:
+
+```css
+@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
+  name: "light";
+  ...
+  --radius-field: 0.5rem;   /* was 9999rem */
+  ...
+}
+
+@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
+  name: "dark";
+  ...
+  --radius-field: 0.5rem;   /* was 9999rem — must be changed here too */
+  ...
+}
+```
+
+Both carry `--radius-field: 9999rem`. Fixing only `light` leaves every field
+pill-shaped again the moment the app is in dark mode. **Change the value in both
+theme blocks** (and in any additional custom theme block the file defines).
+
+While you're there, check `--radius-selector` and `--radius-box` in the same
+blocks — if they were also set to `9999rem`, badges/toggles and cards/modals have
+the same problem and should get finite values too.
+
+After the token is fixed in every theme, remove the `rounded-lg` patches from the
+two inputs so they inherit the theme like everything else — no exceptions, no
+drift.

